I preserved the original LayerNorm, GELU scorer, and earlier ReLU module. I added parallel, bounded corrections for account eligibility, card PINs, and incorrect exchange rates on card payments or cash withdrawals.

The new directions come from messages I wrote, with separate semantic groups and contrasting requests. I changed coordinate units through a decomposition of the existing input weights. I used reference directions, differences of group means, fixed margins, and ReLU min/max circuits. Each correction adds at most 16 to its target department. Construction uses no evidence vectors, check vectors, training, optimizer, regression, or solver fitted to message data.

Forward checks confirm that the compiled network matches the arithmetic rule within 2e-10. All original weights remain in the preserved branch.

Evidence: 14/16 eligibility examples now route correctly; all 16 other evidence routes remain unchanged. Across 168 separate check messages, 65/70 eligibility, 9/9 PIN, and 8/8 exchange-rate cases pass; 78/81 other routes remain unchanged. Some wording still fails. Universal compliance and performance on the hidden set remain unverified. See verification.json and the reproducible construction scripts.
